==== NAME
pdxping -- minimal ICMP echo CLI, the first exerciser of the
R_NET_PRIVILEGED_PROTOCOL elevate class.

==== SYNOPSIS
    pdxping [--count=N] [--interval-ms=N] [--timeout-ms=N] [--dry-run] <host>

Defaults: count=4, interval-ms=1000, timeout-ms=1000. `<host>` is
required; no default.

==== DESCRIPTION
`pdxping` is a standalone ring-3 ELF -- its own `_start`, no shared
library, no dynamic linker. It is deliberately small: one echo per
syscall, one blocking wait for the matching reply, no traceroute, no
MTU discovery, no flood mode (`design/networking/r100-user-tools-plan.md`
§5, paideia-os repo).

At v1.0.0 (Wave AA cohort), only the `--dry-run` path is real:
`--count` `PingRecord@0.1` records are built and their 128 raw bytes
previewed to fd 2 as a hex dump, one per iteration, no network I/O.
A non-`--dry-run` invocation calls the `R_NET_PRIVILEGED_PROTOCOL`
elevate gate before any echo attempt; the gate is a fail-closed WEAK
stub at this landing (no broker-endpoint cap is provisioned to this
tool), so every non-`--dry-run` invocation exits 13 with
`[pdxping.M3-001 EACCES]` on fd 2. Real `sys_icmp_echo` (sysno 103,
landed kernel-side at R100-PREP-003) dispatch is M2 scope, not yet
implemented in this repo.

==== EXIT STATUS
    0   OK (--dry-run completed; every PingRecord@0.1 previewed)
    2   argv error (missing <host>, unknown flag, malformed numeric value)
    13  R_NET_PRIVILEGED_PROTOCOL elevate refused (fail-closed; every
        non---dry-run invocation at this landing)

==== LIMITATIONS
See CHANGELOG.md "Known deferred substrate": M2 (real echo, RTT
stats) is out of scope for the Wave AA cohort; `libpdx-elevate` and
`libpdx-audit` integration are WEAK stubs pending a real cross-repo
link path.

==== SEE ALSO
